  "parsing_gotchas": [
    "page_or_section_count reports Word sections, not rendered pages.",
    "There are nine top-level tables; the first four are PSR, the next three are individual therapy (mapped to OP), the eighth is 1:1 PSR, and the ninth has no explicit OP/PSR label.",
    "The first seven tables have no semantic column-header row. A leading schedule/total row exists in tables 0–3 and must not be parsed as a client.",
    "A global name-header search will miss clients: names are in the third physical cell for tables 0–6, in both third and fourth physical cells for table 7, and both columns for table 8.",
    "Staff names serve as headers in the final two tables; those header texts are intentionally omitted from this structure-only output.",
    "Tables 1, 3 and 4 declare four grid columns, but most rows contain three physical cells. Each has one cell with gridSpan=2; do not flatten row.cells without accounting for duplicated merged-cell references.",
    "The final two tables contain independent people in adjacent columns, not first/last name parts split across columns.",
    "Schedule/summary rows containing parenthetical service labels recur inside tables 0–2. These are not client rows. The final table includes name cells with trailing status annotations after a spaced hyphen; remove those annotations before matching.",
    "Some populated rows have blank names; blank template rows are mixed with populated rows. data_row_count includes populated rows with blank names and excludes schedule/header/summary rows; fill rates use populated data rows as denominator. repeated_header_rows counts recurring schedule/summary rows, not automatic Word repeating-header flags.",
    "The name-format categories describing order are mutually exclusive; ALL CAPS, suffix and nickname indicators are additional overlapping counts. Hyphenated surnames and nonbreaking spaces occur.",
    "Counts of within-table repeats mean extra normalized name occurrences, not distinct repeated people. OP/PSR overlap counts exclude the final service-unclear table.",
    "No automatic repeated-header flags, nested tables, text boxes, images or tracked insertions/deletions were found in the body. Explicit page breaks occur in later paragraphs.",
    "The source package includes custom XML and footnote/endnote parts; the demo is rebuilt into a fresh package rather than copying those potentially sensitive parts.",
    "After the roster tables there are contact instructions, staff names and phone numbers. They are omitted here and replaced with fake text in the demo."
  ]
